# The build context is copied into the daemon before the first instruction
# runs, so anything listed here is a byte that never crosses the wire and a
# layer that never invalidates. Two of these matter beyond speed:
#
#   .env       -- real credentials. Copied into an image, they are readable by
#                 anyone who can pull it, and they survive being "deleted" in a
#                 later layer. Secrets come from the runtime environment.
#   *.db       -- a local SQLite file holds real client rows. Baking one into a
#                 published image discloses them.

.git
.gitignore
.github

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

.env
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.log

# The notebook is committed with its outputs so it reads without running; the
# service never opens it, and its dependency set (a Jupyter kernel, a static
# image exporter) is deliberately not installed in the image.
demo.ipynb
requirements-notebook.txt
docs/
*.md
!README.md

.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
